        "-->\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Plotting the top 3 sources for any state\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's do one more example and create a function that will produce a plot of the top 3 primary sources by number of power plants for a given state.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Step 1: solve the problem for a concrete example\n",
        "\n",
        "We can start with the code we had for California. We will use our `top3_sources` function instead of the code that found the `ca_top_sources` list."
      ],
      "id": "dea211d6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# CA top 3 primary sources by number of power plants\n",
        "ca_top_sources = top3_sources('California', power_plants)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Select CA power plants and boundary\n",
        "ca_power_plants = power_plants[power_plants['state'] == 'California']\n",
        "ca_boundary = states[states['name'] == \"California\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create subplots for each top source in a single figure\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12,6), nrows=1, ncols=3)\n",
        "for axis, source in zip(ax, ca_top_sources):   # Iterate over subplots and energy sources\n",
        "\n",
        "    axis.set_title(source)\n",
        "    axis.axis('off')\n",
        "\n",
        "    ca_boundary.plot(ax=axis,\n",
        "                     color='none')\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Subset power plants by source and plot\n",
        "    source_subset = ca_power_plants[ca_power_plants['primsource'] == source]\n",
        "    source_subset.plot(ax=axis,\n",
        "                    markersize=5,\n",
        "                    alpha=0.5)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig.suptitle(\"Top 3 primary sources by number of power plants in California\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "c1c3312d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: identify which parts of the code need to be generalized and update them\n",
        "\n",
        "Basically anything where we are using California specifically.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. First update all the `'California'` strings to use a variable called `state` instead.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Then, update all variables that have `ca_` to be more general (e.g., `state_power_plants`, `state_boundary`)."
      ],
      "id": "1e9aaad9"
